Subject: [Rprotobuf-yada] How are multiple messages delimited?
Message-ID: <CD51419A.A96E%johansen@adobe.com>

Examples such as the one in http://lists.r-forge.r-project.org/pipermail/rprotobuf-yada/2009-November/000042.html indicate that RProtoBuf is able to read multiple messages from the same file. Is that correct? If so, how does RProtoBuf's read method expect those messages to be delimited? I have files with multiple messages delimited using the PB library's writeDelimitedTo(?) function but haven't been able to read it using RProtoBuf.
Any thoughts would be appreciated.
- Josh
